NET4-F2 is not a harness artifact. It reproduced 4/4 under changed conditions:
- a different build mode: the shared dev server on 5199 instead of the critic's production preview;
- my own child session server on 7877;
- only 2 browsers instead of 4;
- a real F5 (`page.reload()` on the same plain URL and profile) instead of `goto` with different parameters;
- the host passing the title with a real key;
- the Rejoin button clicked with the mouse instead of Enter.

Every time, the host comes back from Rejoin with a freshly booted world (tick 58-60, level null, room 0, phase idle). Every guest follows it into the empty camp with 0 Glint and the third skill gone. No warning or confirmation is shown.

I ruled out each artifact hypothesis:
- **HMR:** tick counters stayed monotonic and there were 0 page errors.
- **Contention:** it happens with only 2 browsers.
- **Input never reaching the page:** net went offline -> host within 1 s of the click, and the click hit the focused 'Rejoin' button element.
- **Wrong port:** the stored session URL is my server.
- **URL parameters:** the true reload of the same URL gives the same result.

